      "writtenOn": "2017-12-05T16:23:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "technically we don\u0027t need a new structure - we could move \u0027thread\u0027 in flat_binder_object, and just store the \u0027old\u0027 size of flat_binder_object. Then new userspace could use flat_binder_object with thread by default, and:\n\nnew kernel, old userspace: kernel sees FLAT_BINDER_FLAG_THREAD not set, uses old size\n\nold kernel, new userspace: kernel always uses old size, this is OK because there can always be gaps in the data buffer - in this case the gap is just the additional 4 bytes of the thread.\n\nnew kernel, new userspace: kernels sees FLAT_BINDER_FLAG_THREAD set, uses new size and accesses thread field safely.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 135,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 135,
        "endChar": 34
